{"series":{"id":"wellbeing::past-year-mde","label":"Past-year major depressive episode · adults 18+ · modeled estimate","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"percent of civilian noninstitutionalized adults","scope":"us_states","definition":"","denominator":"","reporting_period":"2023–2024 pooled","source_url":"https://www.samhsa.gov/data/data-we-collect/nsduh-national-survey-drug-use-and-health/state-releases/2023-2024","sources":[{"id":"samhsa","title":"SAMHSA NSDUH state estimates","url":"https://www.samhsa.gov/data/data-we-collect/nsduh-national-survey-drug-use-and-health/state-releases/2023-2024","date":"Pooled 2023–2024","note":"Adult past-year major depressive episode; hierarchical Bayes small-area estimates and 95% credible intervals."}],"limitations":["These measures describe different questions, populations and time windows. They are not one happiness score.","Life satisfaction is a participating-state optional BRFSS module: missing states did not supply a comparable estimate here. Its curated table does not specify age adjustment.","The depression layer is directly published crude adult BRFSS lifetime diagnosis prevalence, not current symptoms, county averaging or age adjustment.","The past-year major-depressive-episode layer is a separate pooled 2023–2024 NSDUH small-area modeled estimate. Its intervals are Bayesian credible intervals, not the BRFSS survey confidence intervals.","A person can report past depression diagnosis and current life satisfaction. Care access affects whether illness is diagnosed.","The medicine layer covers six selected SSRI ingredients, not every antidepressant. It measures reported Medicare Part D fills by prescriber location, not patient residence or people taking medication.","Drug groups below 11 claims are suppressed. Medicines can have other indications; prescriptions do not establish depression or unhappiness.","Showing these maps next to resource maps does not establish that an industry, resource, or medication caused an ou